---
description: 
alwaysApply: true
---

NestJS backend rules:

- keep controllers thin
- place business logic inside services
- validate all incoming DTOs
- use proper typing everywhere
- avoid circular dependencies
- use dependency injection correctly
- avoid bloated services
- separate domain logic from infrastructure logic

Database:
- avoid N+1 queries
- select only required fields
- paginate large datasets
- use transactions where needed

Modules:
- keep modules focused
- avoid god modules
- export only what is necessary

Security:
- validate and sanitize inputs
- never expose sensitive data
- handle errors safely
- use proper authentication/authorization patterns
